"Birthdirt potion is brewed from the ground of one's birthplace."
"It is stirred with a paddle made from the first tree the person passed under after birth."
"Painted on wounds as a mud mask until it stops feeling warm, it heals bruises and seals gashes."
"Birthplace materials are valuable personal spell ingredients."
"Porti-loth's version is used as a mud bath and drink, with chanting, making the body forget hurt."
"Wounds healed this way do not revert, and a spell of old wounds cannot reopen them."
"The patient must also eat foods native to their world."
